# OpenRouter key, for development only. The site never spends a key of its own:
# visitors paste theirs into the app, and every AI feature runs on it. Locally,
# pasting bygga-dev-mock-key-000000 into the app uses this key instead (never in
# production). The recording scripts use it too: re-record the voice clips with
# `npm run voice`. Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional: the GitHub repo shown (with its star count) in the nav.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GITHUB_REPO=Nutlope/bygga

# Optional: comma separated model lists, tried in order.
# OPENROUTER_TEXT_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5,anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5
# OPENROUTER_VISION_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5,anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5
# OPENROUTER_READ_MODEL=anthropic/claude-opus-5.5,anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5
# OPENROUTER_PLAN_MODEL=anthropic/claude-opus-5.5,anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5

# Feedback (src/lib/feedback.ts): a Redis on Upstash keeps every note people send. Add one from
# Vercel's marketplace (Storage, Upstash for Redis) and these are set for you; `vercel env pull .env.local`
# brings them here, and `npm run feedback` reads the newest notes. Without them, development writes to
# .feedback/feedback.jsonl and production only logs each note (grep the logs for [feedback]).
# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# Optional: the public URL, used for share cards, the sitemap and canonical links.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.usebygga.com

# Optional: hide the manual scanner at /scan. It is on by default.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SCAN=0
